# Image slimming for the hosted demo (spec P6 §3). The VPS has ~23 GB of disk
# shared with the owner's other stacks, so anything the running containers do
# not read stays out of the build context.
#
# Tests never run inside the image (CI runs them on the host), and the workspace
# tsconfigs compile src/**/*.ts wholesale — dropping the specs shrinks the copy
# without changing a single emitted file.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx

# Fixtures are test inputs — EXCEPT packages/ai/fixtures, which the demo reads
# at RUNTIME. AI_MODE=replay resolves AI_REPLAY_DIR (default
# packages/ai/fixtures/replay, relative to the repo root = /app in the image),
# and the demo deploys no OPENROUTER_API_KEY, so a missing fixture directory is
# the difference between "generates instantly" and "falls back to the
# deterministic floor for every draft". The negation must stay directly below
# the exclusion: `.dockerignore` is last-match-wins, and it re-includes the
# whole tree by directory name, so fixtures added under it later are covered
# without touching this file.
**/fixtures
!packages/ai/fixtures

# Prose and process. `docs/` is served by GitHub, not by the app; `.claude/` and
# `.superpowers/` are agent scaffolding.
docs
.claude
career-hq-product-spec.md

# Local tool output that can appear in a working tree.
coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
.vscode
.idea
